Linked at run time, not compiled in
------------------------------------

These are other shared libraries. They are not inside this file. SDS, in
particular, is compiled into StormByte Base, not into StormByte-Crypto.
Each library has its own release archive and its own THIRD-PARTY.

  - StormByte Base 2.1.0 — https://github.com/StormByte-Suite/StormByte/releases/tag/2.1.0
  - StormByte-Buffer 2.0.2 — https://github.com/StormByte-Suite/StormByte-Buffer/releases/tag/2.0.2
  - StormByte-Logger 2.0.2 — https://github.com/StormByte-Suite/StormByte-Logger/releases/tag/2.0.2
  - StormByte System 2.0.2 — https://github.com/StormByte-Suite/StormByte-System/releases/tag/2.0.2

A static rebuild can fold those libraries, and anything they themselves
embed, into one binary. That binary is a different distribution from this
archive, and every notice folded into it has to travel with it.
